{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/197016-lunar-exaltation-homebrew-fluff-old-forum-repost","id":197016,"title":"Lunar Exaltation Homebrew Fluff [Old Forum Repost]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-14T11:34:33-07:00","id":197016,"title":"Lunar Exaltation Homebrew Fluff [Old Forum Repost]","content":"How did Luna create the Silver Shards? Don't ask Luna Vesanus, the reply will answer nothing at all and only raise more questions. Out of what did Luna create her Champions? And, on another tangent, how many Moons had lain in the cradle of Orammus? Was it 300? A few more, adding the greatest Other Moons that make up the Moon Goddess's being? And where are they now?<br /> <br /> Were they made into the core of Luna's ultimate weapons? 300 would be moon gods shoved into a Divine Shard, splintered off from her whole self to become the engines of power to army of mercurial mad demigods.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, it would explain the nature of the Lunar Shard, more self-aware, more independent then the other shards, not completely unlike the Infernal Shards. Each one has its own ideas of what makes a good Lunar; a Steward, a Warden, an Outsider, a Witch, a Survivor or Something Else. Each leaves Lytek's cabinet searching for its ideal Chosen. When it finds a mortal who might have the potential, it settles in and that's when the real fun begins.<br /> <br /> The Shard creates a Spirit Guide, a mask it might wear to interact with the would-be Chosen until Exaltation or failure. As a Background, a Lunar may have a variable degree of continued interaction with this Spirit Guide even after their Second Breath. Now this Spirit Guide can look like many things, depending on what part of the soul structure its taken from. The Shard may choose itself, from memories of past shapes it took or perhaps the Other Moon deep in its core. If it uses the Lower Soul, the Guide may be some bestial manifestation or other natural phenomenon. If it uses the Higher Soul, then it may be a lot of things, something or someone important to the would-be Chosen.<br /> <br /> Through Dreams and Visions, this Guide will then interact with the potential candidate. According to its own whims and ideas, it will test them. Using the knowledge it can gleam from their minds, it will cajole them. It will make them do things to prove their worth, inside their minds as well as in the waking world. It will do this until they have passed or failed. To those who fail, it may be shame and death. In this Age of Sorrows, Silver Shards have left behind just a few Abyssal and Infernal Exalts.<br /> <br /> For those who pass, something greater then godhood awaits. The Shard will truly fuse with their soul structure and a beacon will be sent up. When this beacon is seen, Luna will often have the courtesy to take time out of her day to greet her new Chosen. She has the means to be in two and more places at once, so she doesn't need to drop anything. It's in this meeting that Silver Tattoos and Marks are placed on the Chosen, and she will whisper to them the name of their Guide, which is used as a secondary name for the Lunar. Without Luna, it can be done with the Guide alone, but she prefers this personal touch.<br /> <br /> Now the Chosen's Tattoos normally remain dormant and hidden, only flaring to life when their Mark and Anima is already shining. Their Guide too will appear prominently in their Totem and may color all of their Charms prominently.<br /> <br /> <i>Hidan Gigomori the Hundred Cuts</i> has a hundred rapiers appear in his Totem. He describes his Guide as having been a talking rapier and that when he had been Chosen, Luna took his Guide and carved his life's story into his flesh with only a hundred strokes. When his Anima flares as a hundred blades flaring behind him like a peacock's tail, his Tattoos indeed appear as a hundred cuts all around his body.<br /> <br /> <i>Grisit Lover</i> says his Guide is a beautiful woman he didn't recognize but he believes was the first host of his Exaltation. He describes a very intimate meeting between him, his Guide and Luna and his Tattoos appears as sensual scrawling hand prints, lip stick stains from his head to his unmentionables and his own lips glow silver from many kisses he received.<br /> <br /> <i>Johan the Fountain of Words</i> describes Luna as a wise woman who reminded her of shamistic vows by scrawling them into her flesh while her Guide, in the shape of a geyser, flowed into her skin. Both of these things appear in phosphorous silver whenever her Anima flares into life, melding together in way that cannot be peeled apart at certain strange borders of her body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T01:00:29-07:00","id":197667,"title":"","content":"I like this! I've always been irked that Lunar Exaltation considers so many different things: Nature, Individualism, Survival, Adaptability, Stewardship. I feel like Exaltation, though divine, should consider one thing. The alteration you propose here makes the Shards capable of considering these different aspects, which also befits their magical material being described as almost having a mind of its own. <br /> <br /> I also like that you have Luna giving her Lunars their tattoos. It allows Lunars to receive tattoos without becoming indebted to the Silver Pact. My only complaint with this is that it allows Luna to become the &quot;one good one&quot; out of the Incarnae, who are supposed to be chained in their addiction to the Games of Divinity. Even the Unconquered Sun, in all his perfection, will only tear himself from the Games to speak with one of his Castes, let alone all of his Chosen. But! The imagery you have for the tattoos is excellent! I'd love to see the reaction of an opponent seeing Grisit Lover's tattoos flare up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Burn Legend -- Advent of Yomi Wan <a href=\"http://burnlegend.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://burnlegend.blogspot.com/</a><br /> EX3 -- Dawn of Resurgent Sun <a href=\"https://resurgentsun.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://resurgentsun.wordpress.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3140-greyeyes","name":"GreyEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T16:13:47-07:00","id":198304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreyEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/197016-lunar-exaltation-homebrew-fluff-old-forum-repost?p=197667#post197667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like the idea that Luna takes her time to check in on all of her Chosen, precisely because her nature is more personal than that of Sol. If you want her to be as stuck in the games as the others, simply have the Moon which inscribes the Tattoos be the Shard of a Moon Which Could Have Been which went into creating that particular Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T18:24:55-07:00","id":200629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreyEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/197016-lunar-exaltation-homebrew-fluff-old-forum-repost?p=197667#post197667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this! I've always been irked that Lunar Exaltation considers so many different things: Nature, Individualism, Survival, Adaptability, Stewardship. I feel like Exaltation, though divine, should consider one thing. The alteration you propose here makes the Shards capable of considering these different aspects, which also befits their magical material being described as almost having a mind of its own.<br /> <br /> I also like that you have Luna giving her Lunars their tattoos. It allows Lunars to receive tattoos without becoming indebted to the Silver Pact. My only complaint with this is that it allows Luna to become the &quot;one good one&quot; out of the Incarnae, who are supposed to be chained in their addiction to the Games of Divinity. Even the Unconquered Sun, in all his perfection, will only tear himself from the Games to speak with one of his Castes, let alone all of his Chosen. But! The imagery you have for the tattoos is excellent! I'd love to see the reaction of an opponent seeing Grisit Lover's tattoos flare up!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Canonically, Luna has the ability to be in five places at once.<br /> <br /> And, if I remember correctly, she <i>already</i> personally visits all of her Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T07:59:22-07:00","id":201113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreyEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/197016-lunar-exaltation-homebrew-fluff-old-forum-repost?p=197667#post197667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaint with this is that it allows Luna to become the &quot;one good one&quot; out of the Incarnae, who are supposed to be chained in their addiction to the Games of Divinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like &quot;the greatest gods in the world are all huge cosmic blackjack addicts&quot; is an idea that's been played out a little. Much prefer the idea of UCS still turning his face from Creation due to ancient slights and disappointments, and in his pride and conviction he can't force himself to turn back (or maybe he hasn't been given a good enough reason to). Also prefer notions that the Maidens just aren't that into directly influencing events, for whatever reason, versus being so occupied with something shiny that they don't bother. Being gods, they were created with more inherent Purpose than any other creature existing in Creation; in 2e parlance, while Motivation often (poorly) represents a driving goal for humans, for gods it's a better representation of their statement of being (and thus a much more...inherent part of them that it is or should be in non-gods). So the Incarnae don't handle things in a hands-on way because that's not their purpose, and because it's not their purpose it's also not in their nature to do so.<br /> <br /> Really deemphasizing the notion that addiction to the Games is a moral failing on the part of the Incarnae...that would be great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreyEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/197016-lunar-exaltation-homebrew-fluff-old-forum-repost?p=197667#post197667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Unconquered Sun, in all his perfection, will only tear himself from the Games to speak with one of his Castes, let alone all of his Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>He may speak to all Zeniths when they Exalt, but that doesn't mean he won't speak to any Dawns, Twilights, Nights, or Eclipses at their moment of Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}